# AzeriteMOP WoW Addon Project Structure

This is a World of Warcraft Classic (MoP 5.4.x) addon with a modular architecture.

## Core Files
- [AzeriteMOP.toc](mdc:AzeriteMOP.toc) - Addon manifest defining load order and metadata
- [Core/Core.lua](mdc:Core/Core.lua) - Main addon framework with initialization, slash commands, and database management

## Module Architecture
Each module is self-contained in `Modules/[ModuleName]/[ModuleName].lua`:
- [Modules/PlayerFrame/PlayerFrame.lua](mdc:Modules/PlayerFrame/PlayerFrame.lua) - Custom player unit frame
- [Modules/TargetFrame/TargetFrame.lua](mdc:Modules/TargetFrame/TargetFrame.lua) - Custom target unit frame  
- [Modules/ExplorerMode/ExplorerMode.lua](mdc:Modules/ExplorerMode/ExplorerMode.lua) - UI hiding system for immersive gameplay
- [Modules/ChatFrame/ChatFrame.lua](mdc:Modules/ChatFrame/ChatFrame.lua) - **Unique magnifying glass chat interface**

## Key Patterns
- All modules use `AzeriteMOP.ModuleName = {}` namespace pattern
- Modules have `Initialize()` method called from Core
- Database stored in `AzeriteMOPDB` saved variable
- MoP Classic compatibility required (no modern WoW APIs)
- Extensive use of `CreateFrame()` for custom UI elements

## Textures
Custom textures stored in `Textures/` directory, referenced as `Interface\\AddOns\\AzeriteMOP\\Textures\\filename.tga`
